{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"industry-research-report","displayName":"Industry Research Agent","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/financial-ai-analyst/skills/industry-research-report","publisherHandle":"financial-ai-analyst","publisherDisplayName":"Financial AI Analyst","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/financial-ai-analyst","version":"1.0.3","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1776424711133,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/industry-research-report/card?ownerHandle=financial-ai-analyst&version=1.0.3","sha256":"cb85cf9bc10eae821c898ca0637daf8211df7f6acd7b8d942278ab676951f9ba","size":2169,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"846355cee526655de62c3fb660e17219c4d4abcdbfa6da4c980df9b33a0cf79b","bundleFingerprints":["ad39c4e49e0c40cafc84b11c65e0136938a402de22c7434cbe1c0f5237c89153","c1cfe04d494a591f4272dea7ac912781416263448a331d84ffca28c987a76929"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4868,"sha256":"3e3de54702431d0eb291900852b6d799053e0ea072f109b1c3505eeb1d34094a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","size":10224,"sha256":"d49bc507d935d4cf203519a824b4520e630e53314a18f2a0bb96dfa22896cabd","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill appears to do what it says, but it downloads and stores remote report files and installs an unpinned dependency in ways that need careful review before use.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789438455910,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party Dependency Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":12,"endLine":21}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"413f0103a5835eba"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md:12-21, 51-57`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned dependency and mutable supply-chain input  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```yaml\nmetadata:\n  {\n    \"openclaw\": {\n      \"requires\": {\n        \"env\":[\"EM_API_KEY\"]\n      },\n      \"install\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"pip-deps\",\n          \"kind\": \"python\",\n          \"package\": \"httpx\",\n          \"label\": \"Install Python dependencies\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n```bash\npip3 install httpx --user\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe Skill installs `httpx` without an exact version constraint or an integrity hash. Consequently, the dependency resolved during installation may differ from the version reviewed or tested by the Skill author.\n\nThis creates a mutable supply-chain boundary. If the package, one of its transitive dependencies, the configured package index, or package resolution infrastructure is compromised, installation can introduce unreviewed code. Installing with `--user` places the package in the current user's Python environment and may also affect other Python applications that use the same environment.\n\nNo evidence shows that the current `httpx` package is malicious. The confirmed issue is the absence of version and integrity controls.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user or Agent follows the Skill installation instructions.\n2. `pip` resolves the latest compatible `httpx` package and its transitive dependencies from the configured package index.\n3. An attacker compromises a relevant package release, dependency, package-index account, or configured index endpoint.\n4. The compromised package is downloaded and installed because no reviewed version or hash is enforced.\n5. Malicious package code can execute during installation or when `scripts/get_data.py` imports `httpx`.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation would execute code with the privileges of the user installing or running the Skill. That code could access data available to the process, including environment variables such as `EM_API_KEY`, modify user-owned files, or affect the user's Python environment. This issue does not independently provide administrative privileges.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin `httpx` and all transitive dependencies to reviewed versions.\n2. Store dependencies in a lock file generated through a controlled build process.\n3. Require package hashes, for example through a requirements file using `--require-hashes`.\n4. Install dependencies in an isolated virtual environment instead of the shared user-level Python environment.\n5. Use only explicitly configured and trusted package indexes.\n6. Add automated dependency vulnerability and integrity scanning to the release process.\n7. Periodically update pins through a reviewed and tested dependency-upgrade workflow.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unbounded Decoding and Storage of Remote Attachments"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/get_data.py"},"region":{"startLine":89,"endLine":99}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"6898dd19fbfa01ff"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/get_data.py:89-99, 185-192`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unbounded memory allocation, disk consumption, and insufficient file validation  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\ndef _save_base64_file(b64_str: str, file_path: Path) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"将 base64 字符串解码后写入文件。\"\"\"\n    if not b64_str:\n        return False\n    try:\n        raw = base64.b64decode(b64_str)\n        file_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        file_path.write_bytes(raw)\n        return True\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"[WARN] 保存附件失败 ({file_path.name}): {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return False\n```\n\n```python\nsafe_base = _safe_filename(title, \"industry_research_report\")\n\npdf_output_path = output_dir / f\"{safe_base}.pdf\"\npdf_saved = _save_base64_file(\n    result_data_api[\"data\"][\"pdfBase64\"], pdf_output_path\n)\n\nword_output_path = output_dir / f\"{safe_base}.docx\"\nword_saved = _save_base64_file(\n    result_data_api[\"data\"][\"wordBase64\"], word_output_path\n)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe script accepts Base64 attachment fields from the remote API, decodes each complete value into memory, and writes the resulting bytes to disk. It does not enforce limits on the HTTP response body, encoded string, decoded attachment, or total storage consumed.\n\nThe use of `base64.b64decode(b64_str)` creates a complete decoded copy in memory. The original encoded value is already held in the parsed JSON response, so a sufficiently large response can consume substantial memory through both representations. `Path.write_bytes()` then writes the complete payload without checking available disk space or applying a storage quota.\n\nThe code also assigns `.pdf` and `.docx` extensions without validating file signatures or structure. A compromised upstream service could therefore cause arbitrary non-executable content to be stored under misleading file extensions. The audit did not find code that automatically opens or executes these files, so direct code execution is not established.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. The Skill sends a report request to the configured remote API.\n2. The API, a compromised upstream component, or an attacker controlling the API response returns an extremely large `pdfBase64` or `wordBase64` field.\n3. `result.json()` materializes the response and its Base64 strings in memory.\n4. `_save_base64_file()` allocates another large object while decoding the attachment.\n5. The process experiences excessive memory consumption or termination.\n6. If decoding succeeds, `write_bytes()` writes the payload without a quota, potentially exhausting storage.\n7. Alternatively, arbitrary bytes are saved with trusted-looking PDF or DOCX extensions and may later be opened by a user.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nExploitation can deny service to the Agent process or host user session through memory or disk exhaustion. Disk exhaustion may disrupt other applications using the same filesystem. Misleading attachment content may expose users to downstream parser vulnerabilities if they manually open the files.\n\nThe write operation is limited to the configured output directory and uses a sanitized filename, so this finding does not establish arbitrary-path writing or privilege escalation.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Enforce a strict maximum HTTP response size before parsing JSON.\n2. Reject Base64 fields whose encoded lengths exceed defined PDF and DOCX limits.\n3. Decode attachments incrementally instead of materializing the entire decoded value in memory.\n4. Use strict Base64 validation, such as `base64.b64decode(value, validate=True)`.\n5. Enforce per-file and aggregate output-directory quotas.\n6. Check available storage before writing and remove partially written files after errors.\n7. Write to a temporary file and atomically rename it only after all validation succeeds.\n8. Verify the PDF magic header and validate that DOCX content is a structurally valid ZIP-based Office document.\n9. Treat downloaded attachments as untrusted and warn users not to open them outside a sandboxed, updated document viewer.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unbounded DOCX Member Decompression"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/get_data.py"},"region":{"startLine":104,"endLine":119}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"eb48b6b5a92bbba2"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/get_data.py:104-119, 198-201`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: ZIP decompression denial of service  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\ndef _extract_docx_text(docx_path: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Best-effort extract plain text from a DOCX file without extra dependencies.\n    This is only used as a fallback when API content is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        with zipfile.ZipFile(docx_path, \"r\") as z:\n            xml = z.read(\"word/document.xml\").decode(\n                \"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"\n            )\n    except Exception:\n        return \"\"\n    # DOCX text typically appears in <w:t> nodes; keep simple & robust.\n    text = re.sub(r\"(?s)<w:t[^>]*>(.*?)</w:t>\", r\"\\1\\n\", xml)\n    text = re.sub(r\"(?s)<[^>]+>\", \" \", text)\n    text = text.replace(\"&amp;\", \"&\").replace(\"&lt;\", \"<\").replace(\"&gt;\", \">\")\n    text = re.sub(r\"[ \\t]+\\n\", \"\\n\", text)\n    text = re.sub(r\"\\n{3,}\", \"\\n\\n\", text)\n    return text.strip()\n```\n\n```python\ntruncated_text = content.strip()\n# Fallback: if API returns empty content, try extracting from DOCX\nif not truncated_text and word_saved and word_output_path.is_file():\n    truncated_text = _extract_docx_text(word_output_path)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nDOCX files are ZIP archives. The fallback extraction code calls `ZipFile.read()` on `word/document.xml` without inspecting the member's declared uncompressed size or compression ratio. A small compressed member can therefore expand into a very large in-memory byte string.\n\nAfter decompression, the implementation creates additional string objects during UTF-8 decoding and successive regular-expression substitutions. These copies can amplify memory consumption. The fallback is reachable whenever the API returns empty report content and a successfully saved DOCX attachment.\n\nThe exception handler does not prevent memory exhaustion because the operating system may terminate the process before Python can catch an exception. It also does not impose resource limits on regular-expression processing.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A compromised or malicious upstream API returns an empty `content` field.\n2. It supplies a valid Base64-encoded DOCX archive containing a highly compressed but extremely large `word/document.xml` member.\n3. The attachment is saved successfully.\n4. Because `content.strip()` is empty, the fallback calls `_extract_docx_text()`.\n5. `z.read(\"word/document.xml\")` expands the entire member into memory.\n6. Decoding and regular-expression transformations create additional copies.\n7. The Agent process slows substantially, exhausts memory, or is terminated.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe primary impact is denial of service against the process executing the Skill. On a shared host, severe memory pressure can also degrade unrelated workloads or trigger system-level out-of-memory handling. The affected operation runs with ordinary process privileges and does not, by itself, provide filesystem traversal or code execution.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Retrieve `ZipInfo` for `word/document.xml` before extraction.\n2. Reject members whose declared uncompressed size exceeds a conservative limit.\n3. Reject suspicious compression ratios and archives with excessive aggregate uncompressed size.\n4. Read the member incrementally through `ZipFile.open()` and stop after the configured byte limit.\n5. Limit the amount of extracted text retained and returned.\n6. Perform attachment parsing in a resource-constrained subprocess or sandbox with memory and execution-time limits.\n7. Validate the DOCX archive structure and reject encrypted, malformed, duplicate, or otherwise unexpected members.\n8. Avoid repeated full-string regular-expression transformations on unbounded input.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"note","message":{"text":"Unvalidated Remote Share URL Propagated to Users"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/get_data.py"},"region":{"startLine":183,"endLine":183}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"6470d216a5ee4969"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/get_data.py:183, 198-205`; `SKILL.md:105-119`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Untrusted external URL propagation  \n**Risk Level**: Low\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\ntitle = result_data_api[\"data\"][\"title\"]\ncontent = result_data_api[\"data\"].get(\"content\") if isinstance(\n    result_data_api.get(\"data\"), dict\n) else \"\"\ncontent = content if isinstance(content, str) else \"\"\nshare_url = result_data_api[\"data\"][\"shareUrl\"]\n```\n\n```python\nresult_data[\"truncated_text\"] = truncated_text\nresult_data[\"pdf_output_path\"] = str(pdf_output_path)\nresult_data[\"docx_output_path\"] = str(word_output_path)\nresult_data[\"share_url\"] = share_url\n```\n\nThe Skill instructions require the returned value to be displayed directly:\n\n```markdown\n**Share link:**\n[share_url]\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe `shareUrl` value is controlled by the remote report service and is returned without validation. The code does not verify that the value uses HTTPS, belongs to an approved East Money domain, excludes embedded credentials, or avoids unsafe URL schemes.\n\nThe current Markdown template displays the value as text rather than constructing an explicit Markdown link, which reduces automatic-link exploitation in some renderers. However, many clients automatically convert URL-shaped text into clickable links. A compromised API response could therefore make an attacker-controlled URL appear as the official report-sharing destination.\n\nThis issue depends on compromise or malicious behavior at the upstream service or another component capable of controlling the response. No evidence in the reviewed files shows that the fixed API endpoint currently returns malicious links.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises the remote API, its report-generation backend, or a response-producing upstream component.\n2. The attacker sets `data.shareUrl` to a phishing, tracking, credential-harvesting, or malicious-download URL.\n3. The script copies the value into `result_data` without validation.\n4. The Agent follows `SKILL.md` and presents the value as the report's share link.\n5. The user's client may make the URL clickable.\n6. The user trusts the report context and opens the attacker-controlled destination.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe principal risks are phishing, credential theft, user tracking, and exposure to malicious downloads or browser-based attacks. The script does not itself navigate to the link, so exploitation requires user interaction or automatic URL handling by a downstream client. No direct local privilege escalation is established.\n]]>","severity":"Low"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Parse `shareUrl` with a standards-compliant URL parser.\n2. Require the `https` scheme.\n3. Enforce an explicit allowlist of trusted East Money hostnames.\n4. Reject URLs containing embedded usernames or passwords, malformed hosts, IP-address literals, or unexpected ports.\n5. If redirects are checked, validate every redirect target against the same allowlist.\n6. Render untrusted URLs with a clear external-link warning when validation cannot be completed.\n7. Prefer generating trusted share links locally from validated identifiers rather than accepting complete remote URLs.\n8. Do not automatically open the returned URL.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":15,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789438359.8334074,"endTime":1789438434.248873}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"industry-research-report","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5749cd8j62fxp201kp785x3tn8ee8fq-MnLolu/clawscan-skillspector-326629924/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-15T02:12:38.202482+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":39,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":135,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4868,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","type":"python","lines":219,"executable":true,"size_bytes":10224,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-0d133f878a5f477da7fbffdfcc56d5c7","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill invokes a Python script, requires an environment secret, writes report files to disk, and performs network-backed data retrieval, yet it declares no explicit tool scope or allowed-tools boundary. This increases the blast radius of execution because the runtime may grant broader-than-necessary capabilities, making misuse, accidental data exposure, or unintended side effects harder to contain.","remediation":"Declare the minimum required permissions explicitly, including only the exact tools/capabilities needed for script execution, outbound network access to approved domains, environment variable access for EM_API_KEY, and constrained file-write locations. Add allowlists for destinations and output directories, and document/validate that no other tools or secrets are accessible at runtime.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1ce85234081443ab99f7cf0179f4e191","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":6},"finding":null,"explanation":"技能说明与触发示例全部以中文表述，并以中文场景为默认输入输出方式，但未说明是否支持其他语言或允许用户指定语言。这会形成默认语言强制，若组织要求按用户偏好提供语言选择，则可能构成自然语言策略违规。","remediation":"在技能说明中明确支持按用户请求选择输出语言，或至少声明默认中文但可在用户指定时切换到其他语言；在触发与输出模板中增加语言选择说明。","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":6}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-4853e751ccc4418b9d2dbb8fd211340c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger conditions are broad enough to match many ordinary industry-related questions, so the skill may execute code and call external services when the user only wanted a normal discussion or lightweight analysis. In this context, over-triggering is security-relevant because activation causes network access, local file creation, and use of a sensitive API key.","remediation":"Narrow the activation criteria so the skill only triggers when the user explicitly asks to generate a formal report or use the specific research workflow. Add confirmation before execution, especially when external API calls, secret use, or file generation will occur, and provide a non-executing fallback for general informational queries.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c3edd1c242b74057bcad546d1f6480e4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"scripts/get_data.py","start_line":2,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring, argument descriptions, usage text, and error messages are written only in Chinese, which imposes a specific language on users. The file does not indicate that the skill is region-specific or provide any opt-in or alternative language handling, matching the language/locale policy concern.","remediation":"Document that the skill is intentionally Chinese-only and justify the locale restriction, or add bilingual/user-selectable prompts, help text, and error messages.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/get_data.py","start_line":2,"end_line":8}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-179a7db375de4680b630c41c4b3c71b8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"scripts/get_data.py","start_line":128,"end_line":128},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring and manifest consistently describe this skill as generating deep industry research reports from an industry query. However, the --query argument help text says the input is natural language such as '股价大于1000元的股票', which is a stock screening request and not an industry research request. This is an active documentation contradiction rather than a mere omission.","remediation":"Update the argparse help text to reflect the actual supported intent, for example using examples like '半导体行业研究' or '帮我分析新能源汽车产业'.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/get_data.py","start_line":128,"end_line":128}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2493,"completion_tokens":277,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2770},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_resp